== F. Theorem D: the private-atom bank (from stopping times) on a finite window ==
ok: the orbits of 2..1000 (shortcut map) stay below M = 125252
ok: construction admissible on [1, 125252]: every D_m >= log2 m + 2 (min D_m = 99)
ok: every D_m exceeds log2 M + 2, so v2(n - z_m) = v2(n - m) for all n != m in the window
ok: the finite bank {z_m = m + 2^(D_m)/3, eps_m} (m <= 125252) has -eps_n < Phi(n) - F(n) <= 0 on the window
ok: Theorem D window check: along all 39889 steps of the orbits of 2..1000, R(Tn) - R(n) <= -1.9991 <= -C + delta/2 = -1.9750 (the finite bank is exact on the window; the infinite construction adds a tail in [0, delta((3 + log2 M)/M + 1/(M ln 2))])
ok: height moment sum_{m<=M} eps_m D_m = 7.63e+04, 1.08e+06, 1.36e+07, 1.74e+07 for M = 10^3, 10^4, 10^5, 125252: it diverges (Theorem C)
ok: the shadow lower bound Phi(y) >= kappa (V-1) - j log 2 holds at all 107 points y = 2^j (2^V - 1) of the window
  [Q1 wall 0.5 s]

